.TH NKOSI 1 "2024" "NKOSI 0.1.0" "NKOSI User Manual"
.SH NAME
nkosi \- Linux endpoint security agent

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nkosi
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
NKOSI is a comprehensive Linux endpoint security agent providing real-time
threat detection, rootkit scanning, firewall management, and more.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Display current agent status and recent events.

.TP
.B scan \fIPATH\fR
Scan a file or directory for threats.

.TP
.B quick
Quick scan of critical system directories.

.TP
.B full
Full system scan.

.TP
.B rootkit
Scan for rootkits and system anomalies.

.TP
.B integrity [\fI--baseline\fR]
Scan system integrity or create baseline.

.TP
.B kernel
Scan loaded kernel modules for suspicious entries.

.TP
.B ssh [\fI--threshold N\fR] [\fI--block\fR]
Scan SSH brute-force attempts in auth.log.

.TP
.B firewall \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage NKOSI firewall rules.
.RS
Subcommands: status, init, flush, block, unblock, whitelist, unwhitelist, ratelimit, save, load
.RE

.TP
.B quarantine \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage quarantined files.
.RS
Subcommands: list, restore, delete, purge
.RE

.TP
.B backup \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage configuration backups.
.RS
Subcommands: create, restore, list, prune
.RE

.TP
.B update [\fI--force\fR]
Update threat intelligence databases.

.TP
.B logs [\fILINES\fR]
Display recent log entries.

.TP
.B process \fIPID\fR
Scan a specific process.

.TP
.B network \fITARGET\fR
Scan network connections for an IP/CIDR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help information.

.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version information.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nkosi/nkosi.toml
Main configuration file.

.TP
.I /var/lib/nkosi/nkosi.db
SQLite database for events and quarantine.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan for rootkits:
.br
$ nkosi rootkit

.PP
Block an IP address:
.br
$ nkosi firewall block 192.168.1.100

.PP
Create configuration backup:
.br
$ nkosi backup create

.SH AUTHOR
NKOSI Team
